        "_range_comment": "linkBudget.model='physicalRF' returns PURE THERMAL DLL jitter with no floor: 1.87e-05 m at this 1 km / 26 GHz / 10.23 MHz link (C/N0 124.85 dB-Hz, 99.85 dB margin) - 3-4 orders below any real two-way ranging budget, and the only R in the repo built that way (every other path declares a TOTAL budget; see +revgnss/ISLMeasurementBuilder.m:130). Using model='fixed' instead, where sigma_m IS the total budget. sigma_m=0.40 m is set to COVER the worst per-link uncalibrated hardware bias (0.3897 m on A2-A3 = 0.5*c*(|turnaround|+|terminal|)), which is a deterministic constant this configuration does not estimate. Declaring a smaller sigma would leave a 4.5-7.8 sigma unmodelled systematic on every row; the validateConfig guard now refuses that.",
