        "_schedule_comment": "start_s=600: the ISL two-way range is a RELATIVE observable whose linearization is only valid while the state correction is small against the ~1000 m baseline. The joint EKF starts with a deterministic 1146.7 m position error (config/masterConfig.m:1465), comparable to the baseline, so an early near-exact range row moves the endpoints hundreds of metres PERPENDICULAR to the baseline - first-order invisible to the row, second-order a large self-inflicted range error. Deferring to 600 s lets the ground stack converge first. Measured at 1000 epochs: baseline error 1.6 m RMS (vs 96 m with no ISL range at all) and absolute position unchanged at ~1157 m, which is correct - a two-way range is blind to common translation."
